2
00:07:55,555 --> 00:08:01,555
Predator is a science fiction, action, adventure
film directed by John McTiernan.

3
00:11:53,333 --> 00:11:59,333
A team of elite commandos on a secret mission in a Central American jungle
come to find themselves hunted by an extraterrestrial warrior.

4
00:15:51,111 --> 00:15:57,111
Major Alan "Dutch" Schaefer, played by Arnold Schwarzenegger.

5
00:19:48,888 --> 00:19:54,888
Al Dillon, played by Carl Weathers.

6
00:23:46,666 --> 00:23:52,666
The Predator / Helicopter Pilot, played by Kevin Peter Hall.

7
00:27:44,444 --> 00:27:50,444
Anna Gonsalves, played by Elpidia Carrillo.

8
00:31:42,222 --> 00:31:48,222
Mac Eliot, played by Bill Duke.

9
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:46,000
Blain Cooper, played by Jesse Ventura.

10
00:39:37,777 --> 00:39:43,777
Predator is a 1987 American science fiction action horror film directed by
John McTiernan and written by brothers Jim and John Thomas.

11
00:43:35,555 --> 00:43:41,555
Arnold Schwarzenegger stars as Alan "Dutch" Schaefer, the leader of an elite paramilitary rescue team on a mission to save hostages in a Central American
rainforest, who encounters a deadly Predator (Kevin Peter Hall), a skilled and technologically advanced extraterrestrial that stalks and hunts his team down.

12
00:47:33,333 --> 00:47:39,333
The film also features Elpidia Carrillo, Carl Weathers, Richard Chaves,
Sonny Landham, Bill Duke, Jesse Ventura and Shane Black.

13
00:51:31,111 --> 00:51:37,111
Predator was written in 1984 with a working title of Hunter.

14
00:55:28,888 --> 00:55:34,888
Filming ran from March to June 1986 with creature effects, devised
by Stan Winston and a budget of around $15 million.

15
00:59:26,666 --> 00:59:32,666
20th Century Fox released the film on June 12, 1987, in the United
States of America, and it grossed $98 million worldwide.

16
01:03:24,444 --> 01:03:30,444
Initial reviews were mixed, but the film has since been considered a classic of action and science fiction genres and
one of the best films of the 1980s, and was nominated for an Academy Award for Best Visual Effects.

17
01:07:22,222 --> 01:07:28,222
The success of Predator launched a media franchise of films,
novels, comic books, video games, and toys.

18
01:11:20,000 --> 01:11:26,000
It spawned six additional films: Predator 2 (1990), Predators (2010), The Predator (2018),
Prey (2022), Predator: Killer of Killers (2025) and Predator: Badlands (2025).

19
01:15:17,777 --> 01:15:23,777
Crossover with Alien franchise produced Alien vs.

20
01:19:15,555 --> 01:19:21,555
Predator film series, Alien vs.

21
01:23:13,333 --> 01:23:19,333
Predator (2004) and Aliens vs.

22
01:27:11,111 --> 01:27:17,111
Predator: Requiem (2007).

23
01:31:08,888 --> 01:31:14,888
Schaefer would return in the video games Alien vs.

24
01:35:06,666 --> 01:35:12,666
Predator (1994) and Predator: Hunting Grounds (2020), with
Schwarzenegger reprising his role in the latter.

25
01:39:04,444 --> 01:39:10,444
The film explores themes of guerrilla warfare, central
and south america, predator, trap, alien.

26
01:43:02,222 --> 01:43:08,222
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
